$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(6-(Pyrido[2,3-b]pyrazin-7-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 13 A
microwave tube equipped with a magnetic stir bar was charged with
N-(6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide
27 (50 mg, 0.157 mmol), 7-bromopyrido[2,3-b]pyrazine (50 mg, 0.238 mmol),
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 8.65 μmol), KOAc (1M, 0.40 mmol) and
N,N-dimethylacetate (2 mL). The tube was capped and the mixture was
subject to 20 min of microwave irradiation at 150 ºC. The reaction was
cooled, filtered and washed with EtOAc then water. The solid was slurried
in MeOH and concentrated and then slurried in ether and concentrated.
N-(6-(pyrido[2,3-b]pyrazin-7-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide 13 (32 mg,
63%) as a bright yellow solid. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 12.49 (br s,
1H), 9.64 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 9.16-9.08 (m, 2H), 8.86 (d, J = 2.7 Hz,
1H), 8.68 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.09 (dd, J = 1.9 Hz, 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.91
(d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 2.24 (s, 3H); ESMS m/z 322.2 (M+ + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling, microwave tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structural Basis for Isoform Selectivity in a Class of Benzothiazole
Inhibitors of Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase γ
