$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2
N-(3-chloro-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl)-1,1,1-trifluoromethanesulfonamide
(95 mg, 0.244 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (203
mg, 0.977 mmol), PdCl2dppf (18.0 mg, 0.024 mmol), and K2CO3 (203 mg, 1.47
mmol) were combined in 1,4-dioxane (3 mL). The reaction mixture was
sparged with argon for 10 min then heated to 95 °C. After 18 h, the
reaction mixture was cooled to ambient temperature and additional
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (203
mg, 0.977 mmol), PdCl2dppf (18.0 mg, 0.024 mmol), and K2CO3 (203 mg, 1.47
mmol) were added to the reaction vessel. The reaction mixture was sparged
with argon for 10 min then heated to 95 °C for 24 h. The mixture was
cooled to ambient temperature, diluted in EtOAc, washed with saturated
aqueous sodium bicarbonate and brine, then dried over sodium sulfate. The
solution was filtered and concentrated and the residue was purified by
reverse phase HPLC (35-100% CH3CN /H2O with 0.05% TFA) to afford 65 mg
(61%) of 59. . 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.13 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H); 8.53
(d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H); 8.44 (s, 1H); 8.11 (s, 1H); 7.81 (d, J = 2.4 Hz,
1H); 7.50 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 7.35 (dd, J = 8.4, 2.4 Hz, 1H); 7.24 (d, J
= 12.6 Hz, 1H); 7.07 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H); 3.87 (s, 3H). LRMS (ESI)
calc’d for (C19H14F3N4O3S) [M+ H]+, 435.1; found 434.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane-2-yl)-1H-pyrazol,
PdCl2dppf and K2CO3, Suzuki coupling
