$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Suzuki Coupling. The
boronic acid 20 (2.48 mmol) and K2CO3 (2.48 mmol) were added to a
stirring solution of 2-chloroheterocycle 19 (1.24 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane
and water (10 mL:1 mL). The reaction mixture was purged with argon gas
for 20 min, and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.12 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was
heated at reflux temperature for 16 h under an argon atmosphere. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, dilutedwithwater (30mL),
and extracted with EtOAc (3 x10 mL). The combined organic layers were
washed with water (3 x 20 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and filtered. The
filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was
purified by silica-gel column chromatography to afford 21 as an oil.
2-(Thiophen-2-yl)-4-(4-tosylpiperazin-1-yl)pyrido[2,3-d]pyrimidine (73).
Yield 60%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.99 (d, J= 2.8 Hz, 1H), 8.13-8.06
(m, 2H), 7.66 (d, J=8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.50 (d, J=4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.34-7.28 (m,
3H), 7.15 (t, J=4.0 Hz, 1H), 3.96 (t, J=4.8 Hz, 4H), 3.23 (t, J=4.8 Hz,
4H), 2.41 (s, 3H). MS (ESI) m/z 452 [C22H21N5O2S2 + H] + .
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
