$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2.
5-nitro-3-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-N-((tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)pyridin-2-amine
In a 20 mL microwave vial,
3-bromo-5-nitro-N-((tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)pyridin-2-amine (1 g,
3.31 mmol), pyrimidin-5-ylboronic acid (0.820 g, 6.62 mmol) and sodium
bicarbonate (0.556 g, 6.62 mmol) were mixed in DME (12 mL) and water (3
mL). The mixture was purged with nitrogen gas for 10 minutes. Then added
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (0.574 g, 0.50 mmol) to the
mixture and again nitrogen gas was purged through the mixture for 5
minutes. The mixture was subjected to microwave irradiation at 115°C for
100 minutes. The reaction mixture was cooled to RT, diluted with water
(100ml) and extracted with dichloromethane (3 x 200 mL). Dichloromethane
layers were combined, washed with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium
sulphate and concentrated to give a solid residue. It was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel column using 2-3% MeOH in
dichloromethane as eluent.
5-nitro-3-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-N-((tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methyl)pyridin-2-amine
(0.60 g, 60.2%) as a light yellow coloured solid. MS (ES+): 302.1 (MH+)
for C14H15N5O3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
