$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Isopropyl-6-nitro-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy-[1,3,2]dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole
(15). Charge a 500 mL flask with vacuum dried potassium acetate (37.50 g,
382.00 mmol), 3-bromo-1-isopropyl-6-nitro-1H-indole (10f, 32.40 g, 114.50
mmol), bis(pinacolato)diboron (40.71 g, 160.00 mmol), PdCl2(dppf)2
.CH2Cl2 (12.75g, 15.64 mmol), and anhydrous dimethyl sulfoxide (430 mL).
Warm this mixture with an oil bath to 85°C and allow the mixture to stir
overnight. Cool the dark colored reaction mixture to ambient temperature,
quench with ample water and extract the resulting aqueous mixture with
CH2Cl2. Wash the combined extracts with water and brine. Dry the
resulting organic layer over sodium sulfate, filter and concentrate the
filtrate in vacuo. The resulting impure oil is purified by flash
chromatography (silica gel; load 30% CH2Cl2/hexanes; run 2.5% to 20%
EtOAc gradient in hexanes). The material from this column can be
repurified by flash chromatography (silica gel, 30%-60% CH2Cl2 gradient
in hexanes) to provide the title compound (22.7 g, 68.7 mmol, 60%) as a
yellow crystalline solid.
1-Isopropyl-6-nitro-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy-[1,3,2]dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole
(15). Yield (22.7 g, 68.7 mmol, 60%). LRMS (API ES+) = 331.1 (M+H); 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.32 (s, 1H), 8.03-8.04 (m, 2H), 7.90 (s, 1H), 4.69-4.79
(m, 1H), 1.56 (d, 6H, J = 6.7 Hz), 1.35 (s, 12H).
