$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
N-Methyl-2-[2-(6-morpholin-4-yl-pyridin-3-yl)-5-trifluoromethyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin-4-ylamino]-benzamide
(42). 4-Chloro-2-(6-morpholin-4-yl-pyridin-3-yl)-5-trifluoromethyl-1-(2-
trimethylsilanyl-ethoxy methyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine. To a 50 mL
round-bottom flask were added 20 (400 mg, 0.84 mmol), 6- (morpholin-4-yl)
pyridine 3-boronic acid pinacol ester (290 mg, 1 mmol), palladium acetate
(19 mg, 0.084 mmol), 2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2',6'-dimethoxybiphenyl
(S-Phos) (34 mg, 0.084 mmol), and cesium carbonate (800 mg, 2.5 mmol).
This mixture was suspended in dioxane (2.7 mL) and water (0.3 mL) and
heated at 60°C for 12 h. The reaction was cooled to RT diluted with water
(10 mL) and EtOAc (20 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (20 mL). The combined
organic layer was washed with water (100 mL) and brine solution, then
dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated. The residue was purified by
column chromatography.
4-Chloro-2-(6-morpholin-4-yl-pyridin-3-yl)-5-trifluoromethyl-1-(2-
trimethylsilanyl-ethoxy methyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine as a pale brown
oil, yield 250 mg, 58%. 1H NMR: δ 8.65 (s, 1H), 8.57 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H),
8.00-8.03 (m, 1H), 7.00 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.94 (s, 1H), 5.66 (s, 2H),
3.70-3.72 (m, 4H), 3.56-3.63 (m, 6H), 0.82-0.86 (m, 2H),-0.11 (s, 9H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
