$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-benzo[b][1,4]oxazine
(19). A mixture of 7-bromo-3,4-dihydro-2H-benzo[b][1,4]oxazine (18, 937
mg, 4.38 mmol), bis(pinacolato)-diboron (1.33 g, 5.25 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2
(320 mg, 0.44 mmol), and potassium acetate (1.43 g, 13.13 mmol) in
dioxane (30 mL) was purged with bubbling argon for 3 min and then heated
at 110 °C for 4 h. After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was
partitioned between ethyl acetate and water. The aqueous layer was
extracted twice with ethyl acetate, and the combined organic layers were
washed with brine, dried over sodium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated.
The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography with 14%
ethyl acetate in petroleum ether to provide the title compound. Yield:
(623 mg, 55%), slight-yellow solid. mp: 120 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6)
δ (ppm): 1.24 (s, 12H), 3.29-3.32 (m, 2H), 4.06-4.09 (m, 2H), 6.17 (s,
1H), 6.51 (dd, J = 7.8, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 6.87 (s, 1H), 6.99 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H). MS (ESI) m/z 262.2 [M + H]+.
