$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1. Sodium carbonate (0.575 g, 5.43 mmol) was added to
2-fluoropyridin-4-ylboronic acid (0.306 g, 2.17 mmol) and
2,4-dichloro-5-methylpyrimidine (0.212 mL, 1.81 mmol) in dioxane/water
(10 mL; 4:1), and the suspension was purged with nitrogen.
PdCl2(dppf)*DCM (0.0739 g, 0.0905 mmol) was added, and the vial was
sealed and heated at 80°C. After 3 hours, the cooled reaction mixture was
partitioned between water and EtOAc. The EtOAc was washed with brine,
dried over MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated. The crude product was
purified via chromatography eluting with 1:1 hexanes/EtOAc.
2-chloro-4-(2-fluoropyridin-4-yl)-5-methylpyrimidine (0.22 g, 54% yield).
m/z (APCI-pos) M+1 = 224.0, 226.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, Suzuki coupling
