$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: To 34 (100 mg, 0.292 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (27 mg, 0.029 mmol),
tricyclohexylphosphine (16 mg, 0.058 mmol) and potassium acetate (72 mg,
0.729 mmol) in dioxane (2.9 mL) was added bispinacolatodiboron (119 mg,
0.467 mmol). The reaction solution was purged with nitrogen for 5 minutes
and heated to 100 °C for 16 h. The reaction was cooled to room
temperature, diluted with ethyl acetate, filtered through a Celite pad,
and washed with ethyl acetate. The filtrate was concentrated under
reduced pressure and the residue purified by chromatography on silica gel
to afford
1-(cyclohexylamino)-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide.
Brown solid, yield 68 mg, 0.16 mmol, 54%. LRMS (ESI) calc'd for
(C24H32BN4O3)[M + H]+ 435.2, found 435.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 1-Amino-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indol-4-carboxamide Inhibitors of
Janus Kinase 2 (JAK2) for the Treatment of Myeloproliferative Disorders
