$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compound 22a (General Procedure) Compound 21
(0.102 g, 0.37 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was dissolved in DME (3.5 mL). An aqueous
2M Na2CO3 solution (3.5 mL) was added to the reaction, followed by
phenylboronic acid (0.067 g, 0.55 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (13
mg, 0.018 mmol, 0.05 equiv). The resutling reaction mixture was heated
with stirring at 65°C overnight. After cooling to room temperature, the
reaction was partitioned with EtOAc and water. The layers were separated
and the organic layer was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous sodium
sulfate, filtered, and evaporated to afford a crude residue. This
material was then subjected to silica gel chromatography twice (gradient
elution, 0% to 100% EtOAc in hexanes). Compound 22n Yield: 43% 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.28-1.15 (m, 3H); 1.75-1.66 (m, 2H); 1.89-1.76 (m; 3
H); 2.05-1.91 (m; 2 H); 4.66 (s; 2 H); 7.33-7.22 (m; 5 H); 7.40 (ddd; J =
7.98; 4.89; 0.88 Hz; 1 H); 8.72 (dd; J = 4.89; 1.73 Hz; 1 H); 8.81 (dt; J
= 7.98; 1.94 Hz; 1 H); 9.62 (dd; J = 2.11; 0.87 Hz; 1 H). 13C NMR (126
MHz, CDCl3): δ 23.7, 25.7, 36.8, 44.6, 87.6, 123.8, 127.6, 128.1, 128.2,
129.1, 136.3, 137.4, 149.8, 152.2, 159.8, 163.1. LCMS: ret. Time: 2.14,
m/e [M+H]+ = 320. HRMS [M+H]+: calc. 320.1763, found 320.1764.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
