$DATUM To a 500 mL round bottom flask under a nitrogen atmosphere charged with
3-bromo-5-chloro-1-tosyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (6.9 g, 18.0 mmol),
bispinacolato diboron (6.9 g, 27.0 mmol), PdCl2(dppf)2 (1.5 g, 2.0 mmol),
potassium acetate (5.3 g, 54.0 mmol) and dimethoxyethane (100 mL). The
reaction mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 18 hours. The reaction mixture
was diluted with ethyl acetate (200 mL) and washed with brine. The
organic phase was dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and concentrated
in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography, using as eluent pentane/EtOAc 0% to 20% and then
triturated with pentane.
5-chloro-3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1-tosyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine
(13). Yield: (4g, 50%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) 8.30 (s, 1H), 8.10 (s, 2H),
8.00-8.05 (d, 2H), 7.20 (d, 2H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 1.40 (s, 9H); MS (ES+)
433.
